<A NAME=S9></A>
<H2>Summary</H2>
<UL>
<LI>The dialogue boxes for entries are in one module, <CODE>Entries</CODE>, made with <CODE>Form</CODE>,
each made once and kept in a <CODE>Map</CODE>.<P>
<LI>A list of <CODE>[name, value]</CODE> pairs turns menu choices into values and back.
<CODE>([, x]) =&gt;</CODE> skips the first item of the argument; <CODE>list?.[0]</CODE> is <CODE>list[0]</CODE>,
or <CODE>undefined</CODE> if there is no list.<P>
<LI>A repeating appointment is kept once; its dates are worked out when they're needed, each from the first
date, so the 31st of the month comes back after February.<P>
<LI>Choosing, deleting and dragging are written once, in <CODE>Tools</CODE>, for every section. Each section
records boxes for what it draws, and answers <CODE>describe</CODE>, <CODE>remove</CODE> and
<CODE>dropped</CODE>.<P>
<LI><CODE>wimp.drag</CODE> drags a box and resolves with the window, icon and point where it was dropped.
<CODE>query</CODE> asks a question and resolves with the button clicked.<P>
<LI>A program's own sprites are loaded from a file with <CODE>sprites.spritesFromFile</CODE> and given to the
Toolbar as its <CODE>area</CODE>.<P>
<LI>A ref names its section, so one section can show another's entries.<P>
</UL>

