<A NAME=S11></A>
<H2>Answers</H2>
<DL>
<DT><DD>1  Add the pair to <CODE>REPEATS</CODE> in <CODE>Entries</CODE>:
<PRE>
['Every week', 'week'], ['Every fortnight', 'fortnight'],
</PRE>
and a step to <CODE>STEP</CODE> in <CODE>Store</CODE>:
<PRE>
fortnight: (k, n) =&gt; D.addDays(k, 14 * n),
</PRE>
Without the step, <CODE>datesOf</CODE>'s <CODE>?? STEP.week</CODE> would show it every week.<P>
<DT><DD>2  In <CODE>itemsOn</CODE>, give the appointment's text as
<PRE>
text: appt.text + (appt.end ? ` (to ${appt.end})` : ''),
</PRE>
<DT><DD>3  In <CODE>Tools</CODE>'s <CODE>drag</CODE>, pass Shift on:
<PRE>
org.section.dropped(box.ref, drop.x, drop.y, drop.shift);
</PRE>
and in <CODE>DiaryPage</CODE>'s <CODE>dropped(ref, x, y, copy)</CODE>, in place of the
<CODE>update</CODE>:
<PRE>
const date = D.addDays(a.date, shift);
if (copy) {
  const { id, ...fields } = a;       // all but the id
  doc.diary.add({ ...fields, date });
} else doc.diary.update(a.id, { date });
</PRE>
<CODE>{ id, ...fields } = a</CODE> takes <CODE>id</CODE> out and puts everything else in
<CODE>fields</CODE> (the <I>rest</I>, as in appendix A). <CODE>add</CODE> then gives the copy a new id.<P>
<DT><DD>4  In <CODE>editAppointment</CODE>, add a field after Times:
<PRE>
{ name: 'until', label: 'Last day', width: 120 },
</PRE>
check it in <CODE>check</CODE>:
<PRE>
if (v.until &amp;&amp; !D.parseDay(v.until)) return { field: 'until',
  message: 'Give the date as 25/09/2026' };
</PRE>
show it in <CODE>ask</CODE> with <CODE>until: showDay(a.repeat?.until)</CODE>, and keep it:
<PRE>
repeat: every ? { every, count: +v.count || null,
  until: D.parseDay(v.until) } : null,
</PRE>
<CODE>parseDay</CODE> gives <CODE>null</CODE> for an empty field, so there's no last day.<P>
